basic regex:
^->start of string
$->end of string
[abc]->any one of a,b,c
[^abc]->any character except a,b,c
[0-9]->any digit from 0 to 9
[a-zA-Z]->any letter from a to z or A to Z
\d->any digit (equivalent to [0-9])

+ : one or more occurrences of the preceding element
* : zero or more occurrences of the preceding element

1. regex for digits from 1-10

"^[0-9]+$"       ->any digit from 0 to 9, one or more times
"^[0-9]{10}$"    ->any digit from 0 to 9, exactly 10 times
"^[\\d{10}]$"    ->any digit from 0 to 9, exactly 10 times (using \d for digits)

2. regex for allow all charcters except a, b, c

"^[^abc]+$"     ->any character except a, b, c, one or more times

